cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this pipeline, please cite it as below, and cite the methods it applies (see README.md)."
title: "PAM-Gower Pipeline: k-medoids cluster analysis of mixed-type data in R"
abstract: >-
  A reusable, dataset-independent R pipeline for partitioning around medoids
  (PAM) on a Gower dissimilarity matrix, for data with mixed measurement types.
  It covers explicit declaration and auditing of measurement types, three
  documented routes to complete data, multi-criteria model selection including
  bootstrap stability, split-half replication, robustness across algorithms and
  a permutation reference distribution for the absence of structure, external
  validation on variables excluded from the clustering, and an automatically
  generated reporting checklist.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-13
license: MIT
repository : "https://github.com/DaemSt-James/pam-gower-pipeline"
